{"strongs": "H7921", "word": "שָׁכֹל", "translit": "sha.khol", "root": "שיר", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "be bereaved", "definition": "[ שָׁכֹל , שָׁכַל Lag BN 26 ] verb be bereaved (= Arabic ᵑ7 תְּכוֺל , תְּכֵל ; compare Syriac loss of children ); — Qal Perfect 1 singular כַּאֲשֶׁר שָׁכֹלְתִּי שָׁכָ֑לְתִּי Gen 43:14 ( E ) if I am bereaved, I am bereaved (of father, expressing resignation; on כָ֑לְ see Ges «GKC:29u»§ 29u ); Imperfect 1 singular אֶשְׁכַּל Gen 27:45 ( E ), with accusative of person be bereaved of you both (of mother); 3 feminine singular תִּשְׁכַּל מִנָּשִׁים אִמֶּ֑ךָ 1Sam 15:33 thy mother shall be bereaved above (more than) women . Pi`el Perfect 3 feminine singular שִׁכְּלָה 1Sam 15:33 +, suffix וְשִׁכְּלָ֑תָּה Ezek 14:15 , etc.; Imperfect 3 feminine singular תְּשַׁכֵּל Deut 32:25 +, 2 feminine singular תְּשַׁכְּלִי Ezek 36:14 Qr (see כָּשַׁל Pi`el ); Infinitive construct suffix לְשַׁכְּלָם v Ezek 36:12 Participle מְשַׁכֵּלָה Exod 23:26 , כֶּ֫לֶת - Ezek 36:13 , כָּ֫לֶת - — 2Kgs 2:19 ; 2Kgs 2:21 — 1. make childless , accusative of father Gen 42:36 ( E ), of mothers 1Sam 15:33 (subject חֶרֶב ), compare Ezek 5:17 (subject famine and beasts), and Ezek 14:15 ( id. ; object land); accusative of people Hos 9:12 ( מֵאָדָם ), Jer 15:7 (+ אִבַּתְִּי ), Ezek 36:12 , compare v Ezek 36:13 v Ezek 36:14 (see above); object omitted (subject חֶרֶב ) Deut 22:25 ; Lam 1:20 ; Ezek 21:19 ( Co , for תִּכָּפֵל , see כָּפַל ; otherwise Toy Krae ). 2. a. cause barrenness , or abortion, ׳ הָאָרֶץ מְשַׁכְּ 2Kgs 2:19 , compare v 2Kgs 2:21 ( Thes otherwise, see ׳ מְשׁ infra). \\ \\ b. shew barrenness , or abortion , (1) of any female Exod 23:26 ( E ; + עֲקָרָה ), animals Gen 31:38 ( E ) Job 21:10 (2) of vine Mal 3:11 . Hiph`il Participle רֶהֶם ( וְשָׁדַיִם צֹמְקִים ) מַשְׁכִּיל Hos 9:14 miscarrying womb . — Jer 50:9 read מַשְׂכִּיל successful , ᵐ5 ᵑ6 Heb Manuscripts Ew Hi Gf Gie .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8663')\">BDB8663</entry> [<entry 